<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-8 pb-16">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-6 mb-4 max-[900px]:flex-col max-[900px]:items-start">
    <div>
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Getting started
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.02]">
        Install to first finding in five minutes
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7]">
        ControlKeel turns project rules, domain knowledge, and security boundaries into findings, proofs, approval gates, budgets, evals, and durable context across supported hosts. Agent output is cheap; reviewability, release safety, and cost control are not. ControlKeel governs that loop from the first attach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-0 pb-16">
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">Install</p>
    <%= for channel <- @install_channels do %>
      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border bg-background/70 p-5 transition hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-background/90"
        id={"install-channel-#{channel.id}"}
      >
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between">
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">{channel.label}</h3>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">
                {Enum.join(channel.platforms, ", ")}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">{channel.description}</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-overlay/10">
          <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-foreground"><code>{channel.command}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-0 pb-16">
  <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
    Quick start
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.35fr)_minmax(280px,0.75fr)] gap-6 max-[900px]:grid-cols-1 mt-4">
    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Packaged binary
      </p>
      <ol class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-4">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          1. Run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel</code>
          to boot the local web app.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          2. In your project, run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel setup</code>, then <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel attach opencode</code>.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          3. Binding auto-bootstraps on first use; use
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            controlkeel bootstrap
          </code>
          or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel init</code>
          to do it explicitly.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          4. Run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel attach doctor</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel provider doctor</code>, and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel status</code>.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          5. Trigger a controlled validation, then open Session Control or run
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            controlkeel findings
          </code>
          to verify the block.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Source setup
      </p>
      <ol class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-4">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          1. Run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">mix setup</code>
          once.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          2. Run
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">mix phx.server</code>
          in the ControlKeel repo.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          3. In your project, run
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            mix ck.attach opencode
          </code>
          from the same source environment.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          4. <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">mix ck.init</code>
          is available for explicit setup.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          5. Run a built-in smoke benchmark or validate a pending change to trigger the first finding.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 text-sm">
    Attach defaults to project scope and writes inside the governed repository. User scope is available only for hosts that advertise it. Local stdio MCP exposes the full local tool set; hosted MCP is a separate, narrower OAuth-scoped surface.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-0 pb-16">
  <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
    How it governs
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 mt-4">
    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Governed delivery lifecycle
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-3">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Intent intake and execution briefs at
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">/sessions/start</code>
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Task graph, validation, and findings during execution
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Proof bundles, Ship Dashboard, and benchmarks as evidence
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Proof console loop
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-3">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Session Control for active task state, risk, and approvals
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Findings turn policy violations into reviewable work
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Proof Browser for immutable evidence and rollback guidance
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Ship Dashboard and benchmarks for outcome evidence
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Autonomy and findings
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 text-sm">
        Severity maps to expected human gates; findings stay readable in plain language. LLM advisory is optional and needs a provider. See <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">docs/autonomy-and-findings.md</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Operating modes
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-3">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Local mode ships with SQLite, Ollama, or heuristic fallback.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Cloud mode connects orgs, projects, users, webhooks, and service accounts as shared governance evidence.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Use benchmarks to collect bounded evidence before claiming a workflow is safer, cheaper, or faster.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Occupation-first onboarding
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 text-sm">
        Start from what best describes your work. ControlKeel picks the domain pack, interview language, and governance posture behind the scenes, so non-experts don't need to choose a framework first.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Project rescue
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 text-sm">
        If another tool already touched the repo, bootstrap it, run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel watch</code>, and use findings, proofs, and
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">ck_validate</code>
        to recover. Add governed proxy only when the tool points at compatible OpenAI or Anthropic endpoints.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto w-[min(1180px,calc(100%-2rem))] pt-0 pb-16 max-[900px]:w-[min(100%-1.25rem,1180px)] max-[900px]:pt-0">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.35fr)_minmax(280px,0.75fr)] gap-6 max-[900px]:grid-cols-1">
    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Other supported agents
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-3">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            controlkeel attach codex-cli
          </code>
          installs native Codex skills and the CK operator agent.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            controlkeel attach vscode
          </code>
          and
          <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
            controlkeel attach copilot
          </code>
          prepare repo-native skills plus MCP config.
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          OpenCode is the recommended quick start; Cursor, Windsurf, Kiro, Amp, Gemini CLI, Continue, and Aider use the same portable bundle path.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/aryaminus/controlkeel"
        class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold mt-4 inline-block"
      >
        Learn more on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        What it is not
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-3">
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Not another IDE or coding model</li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Not a prompt marketplace or generic memory API
        </li>
        <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Not passive monitoring or post-hoc review only
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
